Item (1) is implemented in ap/n2ap_venc.[ch]:

  void n2ap_enc_param_1080p30_hevc(struct n2ap_enc_param *p)
  {
      if (p == NULL) return;
      n2ap_enc_param_1080p30_h264(p);
      p->profile = 0;   /* V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_PROFILE_MAIN, mtk_vcodec_enc.c:2760-2762 */
      p->level = 5;     /* V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_LEVEL_4 default, :2769-2772 */
      p->tier = 0;      /* V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_TIER_MAIN default, :2773-2776 */
  }
plus the prototype and a test that checks those fields (and NULL). Accepting: N2TEST V41 PASS 646/646. No other AP change for HEVC; your session profile/level conversions agree with our ven_h265_profile/level table.

Your HIGH joined-header finding: I confirmed the AP cannot fix it at its boundary (the vendor's VENC_PrependHeader memmove runs inside the same AP_IPIMSG_ENC_ENCODE, after its GCE flush). V40's in-flush n2vc_dma_sync is the right place; I noted it in ap/MESSAGE_FLOW.md. Items (2) and (3) are IP's/P03's files, not mine.
